Really, the Nethack codebase does not preclude cross-platform saved
games and bones files.  I took a look at it once, and even went as
far as to write out a plan on how to do it - it's probably a couple
days of effort for a competent hacker who is familiar with the
Nethack code.  The functions for loading and saving a game are
pretty well isolated; the work would mostly just be adding logic
to those functions to store the game data in a cross-platform
manner rather than just dumping the in-memory representation
to disk.

The reason why I never bothered to actually do it is because it 
doesn't seem like something that would really be all that useful.
Every once in a while we see a post like Javier's, but for the
most part, people are able to finish the game they're playing
before switching computers.  Also, now that so many of the
regular players play on public servers, there is even less incentive
to do it.

The fact that those who are currently working on variants haven't
done it either kind of suggests that it's not very high on
their priority list, either.


